    "title": "Exfiltration to a public paste or webhook service",
    "desc": "A command-line HTTP client (curl/wget/httpie) posted to a public file-drop, paste or chat-webhook service - Discord/Slack/Telegram webhooks, file.io, transfer.sh, 0x0.st, pastebin, gofile and the like. These services need no attacker infrastructure and blend into ordinary web traffic, so they are a favourite channel for exfiltrating staged loot (MITRE T1567.004 / T1048.002). Posting a file to one of these from a server or agent account is the signal; an ordinary fetch from a package mirror or an API is not matched.",
